  "reasoning": "Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index rates Alabama at R+15, indicating the state has voted about 15 points more Republican than the national average in recent presidential elections[1][8][9]. With no recent, head\u2011to\u2011head federal polling or updated Senate/GOP primary results available within the last 45 days for the 2026 federal races[10][13][18], the best quantitative baseline is the 2020 presidential result, where the Republican candidate carried Alabama by roughly 62.0% to 41.8%, a margin of about 20.2 points[9]. Given that lopsided recent history, unified Republican control of statewide offices, and the absence of credible evidence of a major realignment, Alabama currently leans strongly Republican for federal elections, though individual races (such as the more competitive AL\u20112 House district[5]) can be less lopsided than the statewide baseline.",
